# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase core, story SKY-002.
NOTE: This story 18 acceptance criteria (> 12) — MANDATORY split required (see SPLIT RULES below).

Generate refined acceptance criteria, optionally updated title/description, and split stories where required. Output raw JSON only (no XML tags, no markdown fences, no preamble) using this schema:
{
  "storyId":"SKY-002",
  "agent":"openspec",
  "notes":"context",
  "acceptanceCriteria":["..."],
  "description":"...",
  "title":"...",
  "splitStories":[{"id":"optional","title":"...","description":"...","acceptanceCriteria":["..."],"agentRole":"...","technicalNotes":{"files":[]}}]
}
Use existing text when no change is needed.

SPLIT RULES (mandatory, not optional — enforce these before refining AC):
1. AC count > 12 → you MUST propose a split. Target ≤8 ACs per split child. Never leave a story with >12 ACs unsplit.
2. Both implementation files AND test files in technicalNotes.files → split into one impl child (non-test files) and one test child (*.test.ts files). Assign agentRole "typescript-engineer" to impl, "test-engineer" to test.
3. 3+ independent deliverable modules with no shared exports (e.g. client.ts, server.ts, cli.ts all in same story) → split per concern. Each split gets the files it owns.
4. External API discovery + implementation in same story → split: first child discovers/documents the API contract, second child implements against that contract.
5. technicalNotes.files contains BOTH frontend/template files (*.html, *.css, *.scss, *.jsx, *.tsx, *.vue, *.svelte) AND build/tooling files (vite.config.*, webpack.config.*, rollup.config.*, package.json, Makefile, Dockerfile, *.sh) → split: one child owns the frontend/template files, one child owns the build/tooling files. These have different runtime roles and different owners — bundling them causes token bloat and diffuse responsibility.
6. Story covers multiple independent runtime roles in the same deliverable (e.g. HTTP server AND CLI binary AND HTML dashboard) → split by runtime role, one child per runtime target. Each child's agentRole should match what it produces (typescript-engineer for application code, test-engineer for test-only files).
These rules apply only when splitDepth === 0. Never split a story that is already a split child.

Story context:
{
  "id": "SKY-002",
  "title": "Implement typed Skyscanner API client",
  "description": "Create src/skyscanner/client.ts that wraps the Skyscanner RapidAPI. The client must: (1) export a SkyscannerClient class whose constructor accepts { apiKey: string }; if apiKey is omitted, fall back to the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable — throw a descriptive Error if neither is present; (2) implement searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]> using the Node.js 18+ global fetch (no third-party HTTP library); (3) export TypeScript interfaces SearchParams { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number } and FlightResult { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }; (4) throw on HTTP 4xx/5xx responses, including the status code in the message; (5) throw a descriptive parse error when the response body does not match the expected shape. Also create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch — no real network calls. (6) Support an explicit mock mode: when the environment variable MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is set to the exact string 'true', searchFlights must return deterministic fixture FlightResult[] data WITHOUT making any network call (no fetch invocation at all) — this is an opt-in-only behavior; when MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API is unset, empty, or any value other than 'true', searchFlights must behave exactly as it does today (real fetch call, real failures surfaced, no silent fallback to mock data on real-call failure).",
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "src/skyscanner/client.ts exports a SkyscannerClient class whose constructor signature is constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string })",
